    "doi": "https://doi.org/10.64599/skds5262",
    "abstract": "The instability of the atmosphere has a significant impact on the development of severe weather events, which are primarily associated with the convective movement of air masses. Local convective processes cause extreme local events such as heavy rain, hail, tornadoes and strong winds. This paper discusses thermodynamic indices of an unstable atmosphere and tornado forecast indices in the context of global climate change. The Tornado Condition Index was used to analyze the Alaverdi tornado that occurred on 25 June 2024. The results obtained showed that the thermodynamic indices accurately depicted the unstable state of the atmosphere (ranging from medium to strong instability) on that day.",
    "field": "Severe weather forecasting",
    "problem": "Forecasting local severe weather events like tornadoes in Georgia is challenging due to the unavailability of direct aerological data and the influence of complex mountainous terrain, making it difficult to assess atmospheric instability and issue timely warnings.",
    "method": "The paper uses thermodynamic and tornado forecast indices to analyze the unstable state of the atmosphere and characterize the conditions that contribute to the formation of tornadoes under climate change.",
    "task": "The task is to use thermodynamic and tornado forecast indices to analyze the atmospheric instability that characterized the Alaverdi, Georgia, tornado of June 25, 2024, within the context of climate change.",
